# EAP reviewer retrieval for retained deliberation (CASE-SLK-2026-88)

context: @oncall22 asked in #support-infra: "Need to reconstruct why the assistant recommended a config rollback for CASE-SLK-2026-88 (RUN-4b8c) to support an EAP review. How do I pull the retained deliberation record?"
@dev_kim: Quick tribal steps below — this is the authorized path. Deliberation artifacts are immutable and stored by month under /evidence/deliberations/YYYY/MM. For CASE-SLK-2026-88 and RUN-4b8c you should find the blob in the March folder.
@dev_kim (steps): 1) Use the internal Evidence API as an EAP reviewer with your org SSO + 2FA. Example curl: curl -H 'X-Role:EAP-Reviewer' 'https://evidence.novatech.internal/api/v1/deliberations?case=CASE-SLK-2026-88&run=RUN-4b8c' 2) API requires the X-Role header and a valid SSO session + second-factor (push or TOTP). 3) Returned JSON will include fields: case_id, run_id, deliberation_blob_id, created_by_model_version, source_refs, created_at, storage_path. 4) Confirm immutability: storage_path will be /evidence/deliberations/2026/03/<deliberation_blob_id>. 5) Verify audit: check /audit/events?actor=<your-id>&resource=deliberation&ref=RUN-4b8c to confirm retrieval was logged.
@dev_kim: Evidence Portal link for quick view: https://evidence.novatech.internal/portal/deliberations/CASE-SLK-2026-88/RUN-4b8c [screenshot: evidence-portal-run-view.png]
@pm_lee: Filing task to add helper endpoint so EAP reviewers can fetch by case+run with built-in audit check. Action: DEV-3427 to implement helper and document steps in EAP playbook. EAP ticket referenced: #EAP-88.

# Proposal: add structured EAP_flag index to retained deliberations (example DLR-2629)

Problem statement:
Our EAP reviewers routinely need to surface candidate retained deliberations during advisory triage. Right now search is by case_id or free-text, which creates friction and duplicate pulls. Example: CS-2026-1302 included deliberation DLR-2629 (an internal run artifact used by EAP to decide advisory scope) and required multiple committee lookups to confirm evidence refs.

Linked deliberation artifacts:
Sample retained-record fields we store: deliberation_id, case_id, eap_flag, evidence_refs, created_by, timestamp, linked_sources. The retained deliberation is not customer-facing and is stored separately from the final answer, transcript, tool calls, source records, and advisory lookup result.
Retrieval path: Engineering Tools > Deliberations API GET /deliberations/{id}; access requires service account with 'read:deliberations' and an audit record is generated.

Proposed fix:
Add a structured EAP_flag index (enum: candidate/relevant/rejected) and surface it in the API index so reviewers can filter candidate artifacts quickly during advisory decisions. Also add a lightweight review_status and last_reviewed_by metadata.

Code snippet (where deliberation IDs are generated):
function generateDeliberationId(caseId) {
  const ts = Date.now();
  const rand = Math.floor(Math.random()*1e6).toString(36).toUpperCase();
  return `DLR-${ts}-${caseId}-${rand}`;
}

Operational case example:
CS-2026-1302 referenced DLR-2629 in EAP deliberations; that run materially influenced scope choices. Requesting feedback on index design, backward compatibility, and UI filters to reduce reviewer friction during advisory decisions.

